            <ArticleTitle>[Transesophageal precardiac electrostimulation in a functional study of the sinus node].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The transoesophageal electrostimulation of the heart has been used to evaluate the function of the sinus node in 103 patients. The artificial rhythm was enforced in 94.2% of cases. The syndrome of sinus node weakness was diagnosed in 32 patients. The transoesophageal electrostimulation of the atria is a safe and simple method for diagnosis of functional sinus node disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
